Empty pairs are text: {//} {**} {__} {~~} {^^} {,,} {==} {++} {##}.

Held: {/i/} {*b*} {~s~} {+ins+} {# c #} {---} {-x-}

The braced form converts anywhere: a {--} b, x{--}y, {--}start.

git log --oneline and --force-with-lease stay literal.

But pages 1--10, the Mon--Fri window, a---- b----- and a -- b all convert.

x ---That stays literal, a-- b does not.

Canonical: <-- --> <--> and <== ==> <=>

Deprecated but still rendered: <- -> <->

Not an arrow: key => value stays literal, and p <= q is a comparison.

x != y, r >= s, +-1, (c) (r) (tm), wait... really.
